A fragmented digital landscape in the style of Piet Mondrian, featuring bold black grid lines dividing the canvas into rectangles of primary colors (red, yellow, blue) and white spaces, where each compartment contains abstract geometric representations of disconnected communication symbols—scattered envelope shapes, circles suggesting conversation bubbles, and angular human figure silhouettes facing away from each other in isolated cells, the composition deliberately chaotic with some grid lines broken or misaligned, suggesting systematic dysfunction within an organized framework, the overall mood conveying structured isolation and the paradox of connected disconnection in a clean, geometric aesthetic.
